Night Wolf Hawk made the next move on the board.

“Tell me something true.”

Cage didn’t hesitate.

“Imagination is not escapism. It’s reconnaissance.”

Night Wolf Hawk’s smile vanished.

Not because he disagreed.

Because he approved.

He asked, “And what have you found?”

Cage looked at the chessboard.

“At the far end of absurdity? Sincerity.”

Night Wolf Hawk asked, “Explain.”

Cage spread his hands.

“If you go far enough into the ridiculous without cynicism, you emerge somewhere holy.”

Jessica whispered, “Why is that weirdly beautiful?”

Micro Nick: “Because he means it.”

Night Wolf Hawk drummed two fingers on the table.

“And if you go far enough into irony?”

Cage looked at him for a long moment.

“You tell me.”

Night Wolf Hawk answered without blinking.

“You either reach freedom… or loneliness.”

Nobody in the booth said a word.

Little Nick slowly lowered the binoculars.

Jessica: “Damn.”

Micro Nick: “There’s the body.”

